# Phase 10 Task 19: the signup-canary cleanup route (group G2).
#
# Import this file inside the API site's route block. Argument 0 is the one
# upstream that serves POST /api/monitor/signup-canary-cleanup. There is no
# second argument and no Python fallback in this snippet: the route has
# exactly one owner at a time.
#
# The matcher names the one path and no method, so a wrong method reaches the
# same owner and gets its 405, as with Python. A trailing slash or a longer
# path is not named here and stays with the site's own fallback.
#
# Rollback is one change: set argument 0 back to the Python upstream at the
# import line. The external monitor, the only caller, is unchanged.
#
# The transport settings are the root/health group's (Task 18): one upstream
# and no passive health, so a refused connection is retried every
# lb_try_interval until lb_try_duration ends, which bridges a restart.
#
# The installed Caddy file is a separate review; this file is source only.
(verdaxis_rust_monitor_canary) {
	@monitor_canary path /api/monitor/signup-canary-cleanup
	handle @monitor_canary {
		reverse_proxy {args[0]} {
			lb_policy first
			lb_try_duration 10s
			lb_try_interval 250ms
			flush_interval -1
			transport http {
				keepalive off
			}
		}
	}
}
